<title>GERMANY: Dyckerhoff says H1 sales up 35 percent.</title>
<headline>Dyckerhoff says H1 sales up 35 percent.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group sales				  1,529   vs 1,130</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p>    --Cement				     700     vs 517</p>
<p>    --Concrete				   350     vs 134</p>
<p>    --Construction products		  370     vs 352</p>
<p>    --Luxembourg				 140     vs 148</p>
<p>    --Deduction for internal sales	 31	vs 21</p>
<p>    Group workforce			    8,888   vs 6,117</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German construction group is Dyckerhoff AG.</p>
<p>Dyckerhoff said it stood by its forecast for 1997 group sales to rise about 10 percent to 3.3 billion marks.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
